{"experiments":[
  {
    "hypothesis":"Spatial beta diversity among reefs within the same region has decreased over time, indicating community homogenization within regions.",
    "experiment_plan":{
      "objective":"Quantify temporal trends in within‐region community dissimilarity to test for homogenization.",
      "steps":"1. For each year and region, create a site‐by‐species abundance (or biomass) matrix with rows=reefs and columns=species, summing across transects.\n2. Compute pairwise Bray–Curtis dissimilarity among all reefs in each region and year.\n3. For each region–year, calculate the mean Bray–Curtis dissimilarity (the average among all reef pairs).\n4. Fit a linear mixed‐effects model: mean_dissimilarity ~ year + (1|region).\n5. Test whether the slope for year is significantly negative (indicating homogenization).\n6. Visualize mean dissimilarity vs. year for each region with fitted trends.",
      "deliverables":"1. Table of mean Bray–Curtis dissimilarity per region–year.\n2. Mixed‐effects model summary with year effect and p‐value.\n3. Line plots of mean dissimilarity over time for each region."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis":"Functional‐group richness (number of distinct functional roles) has declined more steeply over time in unprotected reefs compared to marine protected areas.",
    "experiment_plan":{
      "objective":"Test for differential temporal loss of functional diversity under different protection statuses.",
      "steps":"1. Assign each species to a functional_group using the existing column.\n2. For each reef–year, count the number of unique functional groups observed (functional richness).\n3. Merge the functional richness data with protection_status.\n4. Fit a mixed‐effects model: func_richness ~ year * protection_status + (1|region) + (1|reef).\n5. Test the interaction term year:protection_status to see if unprotected reefs decline faster.\n6. Plot functional richness trajectories over time by protection_status.",
      "deliverables":"1. Data frame of functional richness per reef–year with protection status.\n2. Model summary with interaction estimate and p‐value.\n3. Spaghetti plot of functional richness over time by protection status."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis":"The proportion of cryptobenthic fish biomass (size ≤10 cm) per reef is negatively correlated with mean individual fish body size, and this relationship is stronger in fished reefs than in MPAs.",
    "experiment_plan":{
      "objective":"Assess how small cryptic fishes influence community size‐structure under different exploitation regimes.",
      "steps":"1. Define cryptobenthic fishes as those records where size ≤10 cm.\n2. For each reef–year, sum biomass of cryptobenthic fishes and total fish biomass; compute prop_crypt = cryptobenthic_biomass/total_biomass.\n3. Compute reef–year mean_size = sum(size*quantity)/sum(quantity).\n4. Merge prop_crypt and mean_size with protection_status.\n5. Fit a linear mixed model: mean_size ~ prop_crypt * protection_status + (1|region) + (1|reef).\n6. Test the interaction to see if the slope differs by protection status.\n7. Scatterplot mean_size vs. prop_crypt colored by protection_status with fitted lines.",
      "deliverables":"1. Reef–year table of prop_crypt and mean_size with protection status.\n2. Model output showing main and interaction effects.\n3. Scatterplot of mean_size vs. prop_crypt by protection status."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis":"Interannual variability in total fish biomass at the reef level has increased over time, with stronger increases in variability on unprotected reefs.",
    "experiment_plan":{
      "objective":"Determine whether temporal stability of biomass is declining under exploitation.",
      "steps":"1. For each reef and year, sum total biomass across all transects.\n2. Using a moving window of 5 consecutive years, calculate the standard deviation of reef–year biomass for each window and assign it to the central year.\n3. Merge the resulting rolling‐window SDs with protection_status.\n4. Fit a mixed‐effects model: biomass_sd ~ year * protection_status + (1|region) + (1|reef).\n5. Test whether the interaction term indicates a faster rise in variability on unprotected reefs.\n6. Plot rolling‐window biomass SD over time by protection_status.",
      "deliverables":"1. Data frame of rolling‐window biomass SD per reef–year with protection status.\n2. Model summary with year and interaction p‐values.\n3. Time‐series plots of biomass SD by protection status."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis":"The ratio of planktivorous to herbivorous fish biomass per reef has increased after 2010 compared to pre‐2010 across the study region.",
    "experiment_plan":{
      "objective":"Test for a shift in community energy pathways towards pelagic subsidies in recent years.",
      "steps":"1. Classify each species into two trophic groups: planktivore vs. herbivore using feeding_group or trophic_level thresholds.\n2. For each reef–year, sum biomass for planktivores and herbivores; compute ratio = planktivore_biomass/herbivore_biomass.\n3. Create a binary period variable: pre2010 (year <2010) vs. post2010 (year ≥2010).\n4. Fit a linear mixed model: ratio ~ period + (1|region) + (1|reef).\n5. Test if the period effect is significantly positive.\n6. Plot ratio distributions before and after 2010 and time series of annual means.",
      "deliverables":"1. Reef–year ratio of planktivore to herbivore biomass with period labels.\n2. Mixed‐effects model summary with period effect p‐value.\n3. Boxplots or time‐series plots showing the shift in ratio."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis":"Northern Gulf reefs have experienced a faster increase in the proportion of tropical‐affinity species over time than southern Gulf reefs, indicating accelerated tropicalization at higher latitudes.",
    "experiment_plan":{
      "objective":"Compare the rate of community composition shift towards tropical species across latitudinal zones.",
      "steps":"1. Classify regions into 'northern' vs. 'southern' based on latitude groupings.\n2. For each species, calculate its regional affinity index as the proportion of all its occurrences in southern regions; label species with affinity >0.5 as 'tropical'.\n3. For each reef–year, compute prop_trop = number_of_tropical_species_observed / total_species_observed.\n4. Fit a mixed model: prop_trop ~ year * lat_zone + (1|region) + (1|reef).\n5. Test the interaction term year:lat_zone to see if northern reefs increase faster.\n6. Plot prop_trop vs. year separately for northern and southern reefs.",
      "deliverables":"1. Table of prop_trop per reef–year with latitudinal zone.\n2. Mixed‐effects model summary with interaction term.\n3. Overlaid time‐series plots of prop_trop for north vs. south."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis":"Within‐reef spatial heterogeneity in species richness (measured as CV across transects) has increased over the study period, especially in unprotected reefs.",
    "experiment_plan":{
      "objective":"Assess whether local patchiness of species richness is rising under disturbance.",
      "steps":"1. For each reef–year–transect, count species richness (number of species observed).\n2. For each reef–year, compute the coefficient of variation (CV = SD/mean) of transect‐level richness.\n3. Merge CV data with protection_status.\n4. Fit a mixed model: richness_cv ~ year * protection_status + (1|region) + (1|reef).\n5. Test the interaction term to see if unprotected reefs show a stronger rise in CV.\n6. Plot richness CV vs. year for each protection status.",
      "deliverables":"1. Reef–year table of richness CV with protection status.\n2. Model results including interaction p‐value.\n3. Line plots of richness CV over time by protection status."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis":"Community‐weighted mean (CWM) trophic level at the reef scale has declined over time, reflecting “fishing down the food web”, with the strongest declines in unprotected reefs.",
    "experiment_plan":{
      "objective":"Quantify temporal trends in community trophic structure and its link to protection.",
      "steps":"1. For each reef–year, compute CWM_tl = sum(trophic_level_i * biomass_i) / sum(biomass_i) across all species.\n2. Merge CWM_tl with protection_status.\n3. Fit a mixed‐effects model: CWM_tl ~ year * protection_status + (1|region) + (1|reef).\n4. Test the interaction term to see if unprotected reefs have steeper declines.\n5. Visualize CWM_tl vs. year for each protection status with trend lines.",
      "deliverables":"1. Reef–year dataset of CWM trophic level with protection status.\n2. Model summary with year, protection, and interaction effects.\n3. Time‐series plots of CWM trophic level by protection status."
    }
  }
]}
